[{:db/id 17592186054806 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-17417467-d9e9-5bec-9fbf-80f629e9361e" "question-2bac3c45-54bb-59ba-8dfb-2413c5a3c82b" "question-dd34f23b-b976-5fc4-96ef-147e2f03d920" "question-1343e7c7-8e1d-5ba8-95f9-392742e7c9d0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054511 :question/problem "What is the $x$-coordinate of the point $P?$\n\n![](images/cf/cf628679e0e9726a0db5d3399d992a0333911be16b8ccd89d2d6455e540ea3d9.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of $P,$ we start at the origin, move $3$ units *left*, and then $2$ units *up*. \n\n![](images/2d/2df77be5e817368e4082061f623ab2c10f2ec7f2ebd042864a1418e0aa67592f.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $({\\color{red}{-3}},{\\color{blue}{2}}).$ Therefore, the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is ${\\color{red}{-3}}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054807 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-96d78126-7457-56c7-8793-6786c43a01bb" "question-1b82d2ba-bd69-538e-a621-832dd1619684" "question-373c04e2-db02-5c16-a78f-083cd4605e08" "question-2b4a8301-d80d-5d6b-b666-4d13d2e8333a" "question-becd9473-0ed4-5726-bb5b-2671f06103f1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054598 :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of $D,$ we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point $D$ is $3$ units to the *left* of the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis. So, $D$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3.$\n\nAdditionally, the point $D$ is $2$ units *below* the origin, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, $D$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-2.$\n\nThe point $D$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-2,$ so its coordinates are $(-3,-2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054808 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fbf139c7-761b-543f-b693-759ff9beaf7d" "question-f67f03a1-109e-59a7-989e-ce78b755c960" "question-339cbd4e-71c4-56d8-aa53-97c486b5d7b0" "question-22c2c4da-83e3-5354-8e45-5160f1d5290b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054597 :question/worked-solution "Starting at the origin $O,$ we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $C.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $C$ has an $x$-coordinate of $1,$ so we move $1$ unit to the *right*, in the *positive* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $C$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-2,$ so we move $2$ units *down*, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/49/49069b4b9be29c0a999e7d2b71eec9a973eda9ad1f8a2a7b897d76970771a644.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054809 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fe9f1d19-04b8-5422-924c-2f9a063cfee2" "question-17973190-6a31-5b4a-854e-14acb52dfa7f" "question-7df69925-7109-5250-8a7b-f9894f0d9138" "question-9298397c-357d-5783-87f8-a9a66297312a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054599 :question/worked-solution "In order to identify the quadrant to which the point $(4,-2)$ belongs, we start by plotting the point.\n\n- The $x$-coordinate of the point is $4,$ so we move $4$ units to the right of the origin.\n\n- The $y$-coordinate of the point is $-2,$ so we move $2$ units down from the origin.\n\n![](images/02/02b0dd5d2d125277ffb6fc637fa612eef451c06522efa7655d8374c68641e796.png)\n\nBased on the graph, we can tell that the point belongs to quadrant $\\textrm{IV}$,  the fourth quadrant." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-17417467-d9e9-5bec-9fbf-80f629e9361e" :question/id #uuid "17417467-d9e9-5bec-9fbf-80f629e9361e" :question/math-academy-id "q-61323" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b6fd3712cdcbb16016650ad121a861771b7421b013a37f4cbbf7c94bceaf5085.png)\n\nWhat is the $x$-coordinate of the point $Q?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of $Q,$ we start at the origin, move $2$ units *left*, and then $4$ units *up*. \n\n![](images/2c/2c6371205aa6447e61b6dd675f84df2acb68c3734576b59752b059d338a0b8b4.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $Q$ are $(-2,4).$ Therefore, the $x$-coordinate of $Q$ is $-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-73bf4c34-51a7-5fb3-8292-bc1f98cdd293"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73bf4c34-51a7-5fb3-8292-bc1f98cdd293" :answer-field/id #uuid "73bf4c34-51a7-5fb3-8292-bc1f98cdd293" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1a8226a8-7b9b-5a3e-8f80-cd93f143652e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1a8226a8-7b9b-5a3e-8f80-cd93f143652e" "answer-1335f88d-55ba-56c0-bae1-87c8f865dbe2" "answer-6a2fb253-aa45-58e8-a043-89334f88a84e" "answer-0001803c-afd3-592d-b6a0-b411a5d09ba9" "answer-0d526add-3a91-572e-b501-fd36f94897c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a8226a8-7b9b-5a3e-8f80-cd93f143652e" :answer/id #uuid "1a8226a8-7b9b-5a3e-8f80-cd93f143652e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1335f88d-55ba-56c0-bae1-87c8f865dbe2" :answer/id #uuid "1335f88d-55ba-56c0-bae1-87c8f865dbe2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a2fb253-aa45-58e8-a043-89334f88a84e" :answer/id #uuid "6a2fb253-aa45-58e8-a043-89334f88a84e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0001803c-afd3-592d-b6a0-b411a5d09ba9" :answer/id #uuid "0001803c-afd3-592d-b6a0-b411a5d09ba9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d526add-3a91-572e-b501-fd36f94897c7" :answer/id #uuid "0d526add-3a91-572e-b501-fd36f94897c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2bac3c45-54bb-59ba-8dfb-2413c5a3c82b" :question/id #uuid "2bac3c45-54bb-59ba-8dfb-2413c5a3c82b" :question/math-academy-id "q-61325" :question/problem "![](images/10/10226291288116b0a91ba58fc8d1ee89390965473f914064ee1b6fc386ca04f9.png)\n\nWhat is the $x$-coordinate of the point $P?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of $P,$ we start at the origin, move $2$ units *right*, and then $4$ units *up*. \n\n![](images/e2/e239fc0e990a133f43f77c608a731f23b5afde0e76950480980be368c616f1c1.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $(2,4).$ Therefore, the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4f5fd78-a7ad-562a-a7c0-a2cf50f96545"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4f5fd78-a7ad-562a-a7c0-a2cf50f96545" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4f5fd78-a7ad-562a-a7c0-a2cf50f96545" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a05a0d5e-7d5e-55ab-b362-1360a1187b18" :answer-field/choices ["answer-88d68393-7973-54cd-a373-f5a87981f7fb" "answer-f5c78deb-25be-5ae4-b1f9-903a7ad1f416" "answer-c13fb6af-2b9a-5523-b838-1426dce3a9a9" "answer-a05a0d5e-7d5e-55ab-b362-1360a1187b18" "answer-efab4ff7-734d-5d24-b301-5981ecf76be8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88d68393-7973-54cd-a373-f5a87981f7fb" :answer/id #uuid "88d68393-7973-54cd-a373-f5a87981f7fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5c78deb-25be-5ae4-b1f9-903a7ad1f416" :answer/id #uuid "f5c78deb-25be-5ae4-b1f9-903a7ad1f416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c13fb6af-2b9a-5523-b838-1426dce3a9a9" :answer/id #uuid "c13fb6af-2b9a-5523-b838-1426dce3a9a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a05a0d5e-7d5e-55ab-b362-1360a1187b18" :answer/id #uuid "a05a0d5e-7d5e-55ab-b362-1360a1187b18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efab4ff7-734d-5d24-b301-5981ecf76be8" :answer/id #uuid "efab4ff7-734d-5d24-b301-5981ecf76be8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/valida