s shown on the axes above. To which quadrant does it belong?" :question/worked-solution "We label the quadrants as follows:\n\n![](images/77/77a74e78ea9c1d880083eb9868d42d547549af73395003ecab4c08d96ce75fe7.png)\n\nSince $B$ is placed above and to the left of the origin, it lies in quadrant $\\text{II},$ which is the second quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0f8a175c-5cea-592c-9a16-dbcd9b012fa6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0f8a175c-5cea-592c-9a16-dbcd9b012fa6" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f8a175c-5cea-592c-9a16-dbcd9b012fa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6b29aa89-e385-5dc5-9891-e712c71032ab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-40c0080a-2057-5ae3-958c-5ce297522af4" "answer-3be94df4-6fff-56cc-b61c-1c9be533a501" "answer-27633f58-a6d2-5307-bd31-29b1cab88ef1" "answer-6b29aa89-e385-5dc5-9891-e712c71032ab" "answer-3ffbcafc-4e15-5257-ad1c-619b9e1498a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40c0080a-2057-5ae3-958c-5ce297522af4" :answer/id #uuid "40c0080a-2057-5ae3-958c-5ce297522af4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "First quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3be94df4-6fff-56cc-b61c-1c9be533a501" :answer/id #uuid "3be94df4-6fff-56cc-b61c-1c9be533a501" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Fourth quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27633f58-a6d2-5307-bd31-29b1cab88ef1" :answer/id #uuid "27633f58-a6d2-5307-bd31-29b1cab88ef1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Left quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b29aa89-e385-5dc5-9891-e712c71032ab" :answer/id #uuid "6b29aa89-e385-5dc5-9891-e712c71032ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Second quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ffbcafc-4e15-5257-ad1c-619b9e1498a0" :answer/id #uuid "3ffbcafc-4e15-5257-ad1c-619b9e1498a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Third quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7df69925-7109-5250-8a7b-f9894f0d9138" :question/id #uuid "7df69925-7109-5250-8a7b-f9894f0d9138" :question/math-academy-id "q-109032" :question/problem "![](images/69/697a2ef3438aaea021f0886e1172019744c643acc4195daf126e6f64d0a77917.png)\n\nA point $T$ is shown on the axis above. To which quadrant does it belong?" :question/worked-solution "We label the quadrants as follows:\n\n![](images/41/41a419063ce1bc160023de139406c6ed8f66ab4f7046f223386fc5d93dd60292.png)\n\nSince $T$ is placed below and to the right of the origin, it lies in quadrant $\\text{IV},$ which is the fourth quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4e735110-c8f5-5739-8f8c-19b739dad41c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4e735110-c8f5-5739-8f8c-19b739dad41c" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e735110-c8f5-5739-8f8c-19b739dad41c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f7b15fa-1729-5fc5-b5a4-592994262f2b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1fa855f-ae98-5848-8ed4-5d69bbecef4f" "answer-3f7b15fa-1729-5fc5-b5a4-592994262f2b" "answer-87bbd1b5-1a54-5c0a-a789-4768ef2154a2" "answer-0c319688-ec59-54b8-ab54-5271da97c349" "answer-137ff576-efaa-55f1-af2e-f0073467416c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1fa855f-ae98-5848-8ed4-5d69bbecef4f" :answer/id #uuid "e1fa855f-ae98-5848-8ed4-5d69bbecef4f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "First quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f7b15fa-1729-5fc5-b5a4-592994262f2b" :answer/id #uuid "3f7b15fa-1729-5fc5-b5a4-592994262f2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Fourth quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87bbd1b5-1a54-5c0a-a789-4768ef2154a2" :answer/id #uuid "87bbd1b5-1a54-5c0a-a789-4768ef2154a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Right quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c319688-ec59-54b8-ab54-5271da97c349" :answer/id #uuid "0c319688-ec59-54b8-ab54-5271da97c349" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Second quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-137ff576-efaa-55f1-af2e-f0073467416c" :answer/id #uuid "137ff576-efaa-55f1-af2e-f0073467416c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Third quadrant" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9298397c-357d-5783-87f8-a9a66297312a" :question/id #uuid "9298397c-357d-5783-87f8-a9a66297312a" :question/math-academy-id "q-169184" :question/problem "![](images/92/928b00ea1ac59e758c4bc9e224d2d27e1c2149e31d0c5c3ab7673ee9abeae208.png)\n\nWhich of the following is true regarding the point $S?$\n\nI. It is in the fourth quadrant\n\nII. Its $x$-coordinate is $1$\n\nIII. Its $y$-coordinate is $-3$" :question/worked-solution "The point $S$ is in the third quadrant, so statement I is false.\n\nTo find the coordinates of the point $S,$ we start at the origin, move $1$ units *left*, and then $3$ units *down*. \n\n![](images/f1/f150eac73755dc5f39b499b6ca0ba12624e4c27dd79e7207e11f6c88d04b596d.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $(-1,-3).$ Hence, statement II is false and statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-682709b3-961f-5951-9e4b-89301f1f85e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-682709b3-961f-5951-9e4b-89301f1f85e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "682709b3-961f-5951-9e4b-89301f1f85e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a59951d6-4b9c-5418-b347-b1c451db5a4c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dfd571c3-4c79-5b1e-a642-61dd8d70ab4a" "answer-9a6bb31c-d014-567f-ba52-e3afe3919115" "answer-2783bd40-3420-50d6-aca2-a036799a1989" "answer-6fd7f4c1-76d8-526f-9246-9518fbcd5a65" "answer-a59951d6-4b9c-5418-b347-b1c451db5a4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfd571c3-4c79-5b1e-a642-61dd8d70ab4a" :answer/id #uuid "dfd571c3-4c79-5b1e-a642-61dd8d70ab4a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and  III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a6bb31c-d014-567f-ba52-e3afe3919115" :answer/id #uuid "9a6bb31c-d014-567f-ba52-e3afe3919115" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2783bd40-3420-50d6-aca2-a036799a1989" :answer/id #uuid "2783bd40-3420-50d6-aca2-a036799a1989" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fd7f4c1-76d8-526f-9246-9518fbcd5a65" :answer/id #uuid "6fd7f4c1-76d8-526f-9246-9518fbcd5a65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a59951d6-4b9c-5418-b347-b1c451db5a4c" :answer/id #uuid "a59951d6-4b9c-5418-b347-b1c451db5a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055942 :tutorial/content "The **Cartesian coordinate system** (or **Cartesian plane**) is a grid that we can use to understand where certain objects lie, similar to a map. This grid looks as follows:\n\n![](images/fd/fd702a53ff1127a2432cbdd9a3c7057a08c73ac7a086454c066fa2c96bea7974.png)\n\nIt consists of a horizontal number line called the **$x$-axis** and a vertical number line called the **$y$-axis**.\n\nThe **origin** is the location where the $x$ and $y$ axes meet and is given the symbol $O.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055943 :tutorial/content "Every location on the Cartesian plane is called a **point**. Every point is identified using an $x$**-coordinate** and a $y$**-coordinate**. Together, points are expressed using an **ordered pair** of **coordinates** $(x,y).$\n\nFor example, we can mark (or **plot**) the point $A$ with coordinates $({\\color{red}{3}},{\\color{blue}{2}})$ by starting from $O$ and then traveling $\\color{red}3$ units towards the right, followed $\\color{blue}2$ units up.\n\n![](images/c1/c1ef61dedbbcc6eedcd125c2c62cdfbaa4d9b9a12f10181714b51c060a059fd3.png)\n\nWe say that\n\n- the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $3$,\n\n- the $y$-coordinate of $A$ is $2$,\n\n- the $xy$-coordinates (or just \"the coordinates\") of $A$ are $(3,2).$\n\nThe letter $A$ is just a label for our point. It's usually a good idea to label points!" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055957 :tutorial/content "Remember that a coordinate plane is made by two number lines that meet at $0.$ Since these are number lines, we can extend both to include negative numbers.\n\n![](images/f1/f1eeb7f3bc0ab8b39e9dc7127d76a32f1dd130d380748fedc6e11b967f3878ed.png)\n\nWe plot an ordered pair $({\\color{red}x},{\\color{blue}y})$ similar to before, but if the number is negative, we reverse the direction. So, starting at the origin:\n\n- if the first number is positive, move that number of places *right* along the $\\color{red}x$-axis. If its negative, move *left*.\n\n- if the second number is positive, move that number of places *up* along the $\\color{blue}y$-axis. If its negative, move *down*.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find the coordinates of the point $Q$ above.\n\nTo find the coordinates of $Q,$ we start at the origin, move $\\color{red}3$ units *left*, and then $\\color{blue}2$ units *down*. \n\n![](images/b4/b4f58f0c1ad6dc2936ed1b24c844fa82c1b1d5ec10c80e14c6a43f6f4eaf5544.png)\n\nSince we move left, the $\\color{red}x$-coordinate is negative, and since we move down, the $\\color{blue}y$-coordinate is negative.\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $Q$ are $({\\color{red}{-3}},{\\color{blue}{-2}}).$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055958 :tutorial/content "The axes split the coordinate plane into four parts, called **quadrants**.\n\n![](images/93/938125e855fcb96f743c01f2a00d289ef13e0601772bab56cf0f255e9adf4dcd.png)\n\nGoing counter-clockwise, it's common to call\n\n- the top-right quadrant the first quadrant (I),\n\n- the top-left is the second quadrant (II),\n\n- the bottom-left is the third quadrant (III),\n\n- and and bottom-right is the fourth quadrant (IV).\n\nTo remember the order of the quadrants, it's helpful to think about writing the letter \"C\" in the graph:\n\n![](images/1e/1ef91f2bc25ea8b887ec449d2dafe2eaf6a157733e7bc50e4480280df8190728.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054933 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
